  "notes": "USAGE:\n{欲張|よくば}り can function as both a noun (a greedy person) and a na-adjective ({欲張|よくば}りな). It carries a mildly negative connotation but is common in everyday speech, including when teasing someone lightheartedly.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {欲張|よくば}りな{人|ひと} (a greedy person)\n- {欲張|よくば}りなことを{言|い}う (to say greedy things)\n- {欲張|よくば}りすぎる (to be too greedy)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\nThe verb {欲張|よくば}る means \"to be greedy\" or \"to want too much.\" {貪欲|どんよく} is a more formal and stronger term for greed.",
